      }
    },
    "preferred_description_seasoned": "Zucchini grows best in deep, fertile loam that holds steady moisture yet drains freely. Work several inches of compost or well-rotted manure into the bed before planting, since these are organic-matter-hungry plants. Raised beds or mounded hills improve drainage and warm the soil faster in spring. Sandy loams warm early and suit the earliest sowings, while heavy clay holds water and invites root and crown rot, so amend it generously or grow in raised beds."
  },
