      }
    },
    "note_seasoned": "Zucchini does best in slightly acidic to neutral soil, around pH 6.0 to 6.5. It tolerates a wider band, roughly 5.8 to 7.5, and still produces in mildly alkaline soil, though uptake of iron and manganese tightens as pH climbs. A soil test is the only reliable guide before adding lime or sulfur."
